#: ../../../sensors.md:1
msgid "Sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:3
msgid ""
"**Note:** This tutorial is a continuation from the [Moving the robot "
"tutorial](moving_robot)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:6
msgid ""
"In this tutorial we will learn how to add sensors to our robot and to other "
"models in our world. We will use three different sensors: an IMU sensor, a "
"Contact sensor and a Lidar sensor. We will also learn how to launch multiple "
"tasks with just one file using `ign_launch`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:11
msgid ""
"You can find the final world of this tutorial [here](https://github.com/"
"ignitionrobotics/docs/blob/master/dome/tutorials/sensors/sensor_tutorial.sdf)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:13
msgid "IMU sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:15
msgid ""
"The inertial measurement unit (IMU) outputs the `orientation` of our robot "
"in quaternions, the `angular_velocity` in the three axes (X, Y, Z), and the "
"`linear_acceleration` in the three axes. Let's use our [moving_robot.sdf]"
"(https://github.com/ignitionrobotics/docs/blob/master/dome/tutorials/"
"moving_robot/moving_robot.sdf) world and modify it. Create a new file "
"`sensor_tutorial.sdf` and add the code from `moving_robot.sdf` to it. To "
"define the `IMU` sensor add this code under the `<world>` tag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:22
msgid ""
"<plugin filename=\"libignition-gazebo-imu-system.so\"\n"
"        name=\"ignition::gazebo::systems::Imu\">\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:28
msgid ""
"This code defines the `IMU` sensor plugin to be used in our world. Now we "
"can add the `IMU` sensor to our robot as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:31
msgid ""
"<sensor name=\"imu_sensor\" type=\"imu\">\n"
"    <always_on>1</always_on>\n"
"    <update_rate>1</update_rate>\n"
"    <visualize>true</visualize>\n"
"    <topic>imu</topic>\n"
"</sensor>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:40
msgid ""
"The sensor is usually added to one of the links of our model; we added  it "
"under the `chassis` link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:43
msgid "Let's describe the tags:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:45
msgid ""
"`<always_on>` if true the sensor will always be updated according to the "
"update rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:47
msgid "`<update_rate>` the frequency at which the sensor data is generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:48
msgid "`<visualize>` if true the sensor is visualized in the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:49
msgid "`<topic>` name of the topic on which data is published."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:51
msgid "**Note:** Not all the tags are supported for all sensors yet."
msgstr ""

